  <h2 id="who-pays">Who pays for data scientists and software engineers, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    At a services company the client pays the company from the project bill, and your pay follows your grade. At a GCC the parent company's business teams pay, and at a product company the customers who buy the product pay. On the independent route, the payer is a local business owner who wants an app built or numbers explained.
  </p>

  <p>
    A software engineer is checked on a coding round, a design round and work that runs. A data scientist is checked on SQL, statistics and one project where the finding changed a decision. The first basic skill for both is to state your result in one line with a number, such as hours saved or errors cut, and to ask for the pay band before the offer talk.
  </p>

  <h2 id="adjacent-roles">Adjacent roles with higher reported pay</h2>

  <p>
    Some of the higher figures in the 2026 reports belong to roles that sit between the two careers. The study below does not list data scientist or software engineer pay, so set these beside the senior bands above as direction only.
  </p>

  <div class="feature-grid">
