      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <p class="note-line">
    Source: 1 Finance study (Global Economic Outlook Report 2026, with Team Lease RegTech data), reported by Business Today on 12 June 2026. These are broad averages for experienced people, not offers for freshers.
  </p>

  <div class="comparison-grid">
    <div class="compare-card compare-card--teal">
      <div class="compare-card__label">If you lean to software engineering</div>
      <ul>
        <li>Build system design and cloud skill, the areas product-company interviews test.</li>
        <li>Add applied AI work, such as building features on top of language models, to move toward the GCC premium.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="compare-card compare-card--gold">
      <div class="compare-card__label">If you lean to data science</div>
      <ul>
        <li>Get one model running inside a real product or process, not only in a notebook, because that is what GCCs and product firms pay extra for.</li>
        <li>Add a domain, such as banking or health, so you can explain what the model changes for the business.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p>
    A data analyst job is a lower-entry step toward the data side. Our comparison of <a href="/blog/skills/data-analyst-vs-software-engineer-salary-india/">data analyst vs software engineer salary in India</a> shows how that route pays.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai-and-pay">How AI changes the pay gap</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools now draft routine code and tests for engineers, and basic queries, charts and first-pass analysis for data scientists. That squeezes the easy entry tasks in both careers. The pay premium in the sources above goes to the other end: people who build, run and check AI systems, or who design larger systems.
  </p>

  <p>
    Start now by using AI inside your current work, keeping a record of what it improved, checking every output and keeping company or client data private. Later, as more employers build AI features, move toward roles that own the model or the system. Tool use alone does not raise pay without proof and the judgment to catch a wrong answer.
  </p>

  <h2 id="check-before-you-commit">Check before you commit</h2>

  <p>
    The four questions test whether a lane suits your life, and the three proofs test whether you can show real work, so use both before you spend money or years on either lane. The lane you can prove becomes the start of a high-income skill portfolio, which is what employers can check, though it does not guarantee a higher offer.
  </p>

  <h3>Four questions</h3>

  <div class="protocol-stack">
    {checkpointItems.map((item) => (
