          <div class="checkpoint__note">{item.note}</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <h3>Three proofs</h3>

  <div class="gates-block">
    <p class="gates-block__title">
      Pass all three before you pay for a course or switch careers. Free YouTube lessons, official documentation and open datasets are enough to produce them, and an internship or open-source work adds real feedback.
    </p>
    <div class="gates-row">
      <div class="gate">
        <span class="gate__num">Proof 1</span>
        <span class="gate__name">Show it</span>
        <p>
          Software: put one working tool online with its code and a short readme on GitHub. Data: take a public dataset, find one thing that changes a decision, and write it on one page with a chart. Keep it all on one proof shelf.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="gate">
        <span class="gate__num">Proof 2</span>
        <span class="gate__name">Say it</span>
        <p>
          Tell the story aloud for two minutes with no script: the problem, your part, how you checked it and what changed. Practise in clear English, because interviews in both careers test how well you explain.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="gate">
        <span class="gate__num">Proof 3</span>
        <span class="gate__name">Get it checked</span>
        <p>
          Message a working engineer or analyst with one specific observation about their field, a link to your work and one small question, such as whether it would get you shortlisted. Fix what they name, then show it again.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

